(
========================================================================
 PUZZLESCRIPT NEXT EXTENSIONS TUTORIAL - MESSAGING & FLOW
 This is NOT vanilla PuzzleScript, and not quite PuzzleScript+ either.
 Paste it into the PuzzleScript Next editor (david-pfx/PuzzleScriptNext
 on GitHub, hosted from that repo's README) - it will NOT compile at
 puzzlescript.net or in a plain PuzzleScript+ editor, since every
 feature below is a Next-only addition on top of PS+.

 Read puzzlescript_tutorial_4_messaging.pss AND puzzlescript_plus_
 messaging.pss (both in this repo) FIRST. PuzzleScript Next is a
 direct successor to PS+ and keeps everything from it working
 unchanged: level_select/section/goto, runtime_metadata_twiddling
 (noundo/norestart set/wipe/default from a rule), the in-rule undo/
 nosave/quit commands, message_text_align and friends. This file
 covers ONLY what Next adds on top of THAT, checked against david-
 pfx/PuzzleScriptNext's own engine source, not guessed from memory.

 TUTORIAL MAP -- Ctrl+F for a tag like [T3] to jump straight to it.

 [T1] LINK: a whole new way to jump between sections, tied to
      touching a specific OBJECT rather than an unconditional
      redirect or a menu pick - level branching, PS+ never had this
 [T2] enable_pause: Escape now opens a real pause menu instead of
      just dropping straight back to the title screen
 [T3] allow_undo_level: lets Z rewind back across a level boundary
      into the level you just finished, instead of stopping cold the
      moment a new level starts
 [T4] status / status_line: a persistent on-screen status line,
      set from a rule - different from MESSAGE, which is a modal
      popup that pauses the game until dismissed
 [T5] grab bag: everything else Next adds (gosub, log, afx, mouse_
      clicks, auto_level_titles, title/author/keyhint colors,
      export_options) plus a reminder of what still just works,
      unchanged, from the PS+ file
========================================================================
)

title PuzzleScript Next Extensions - Messaging & Flow Tutorial
author Claude, for Gail

( [T2] -- Escape opens a pause menu instead of returning straight to  )
( the title screen. )
enable_pause

( [T3] -- lets undo rewind back across a level boundary; see [T3].    )
allow_undo_level

( [T4] -- turns on the persistent status-line display the "status"    )
( in-rule command below writes to. )
status_line

