RULES
========================================================================

( [T1] LINK: level branching tied to touching an object -------------- )
( The LEVELS section below has a line reading "link Portal GrabBag"    )
( sitting directly above this section's own level - that's what tells )
( Next that touching a Portal object anywhere in THIS level should be  )
( able to jump to the GrabBag section. This rule is what actually      )
( fires that jump the moment you touch it: )

[ Player Portal ] -> [ Player Portal ] link

( -- next: [T4], since [T2] and [T3] are both Prelude-only switches -  )
( see their comments up top and their levels below. )

( [T4] status / status_line: a persistent status line, not a popup ---- )
( "message" pauses the whole game until you dismiss it. "status" just   )
( writes text to a small always-on readout and lets you keep playing - )
( status_line up in the Prelude is what makes that readout visible at  )
( all. )

[ Player Beacon ] -> [ Player Beacon ] status Beacon touched - this line updates live and never blocks you.

========================================================================
WINCONDITIONS
========================================================================

Some Player on Exit

========================================================================
LEVELS
========================================================================

link Portal GrabBag

section LinkDemo

#########
#P..l..d#
#########
MESSAGE [T1]: touching that Portal tile should have jumped you straight to the GrabBag section below, skipping Pause/UndoLevel/Status entirely - a LINK jump, not a menu pick and not an unconditional LEVELS-list goto.

MESSAGE [T1] continued: reading this instead means you reached the Exit without stepping on the Portal - go back and actually touch it to see the jump. Either way, the Exit from here continues normally into Pause.

section Pause

#########
#P......#
#......d#
#########
MESSAGE [T2]: enable_pause is on, so Escape now opens an actual pause menu instead of just bailing to the title screen the way plain PuzzleScript(+) always has. Try it before moving on.

section UndoLevel

#######
#P....#
#....d#
#######
MESSAGE [T3] part 1: remember this room, then reach the Exit.

#######
#P....#
#....d#
#######
MESSAGE [T3] part 2: now hold undo (Z) down. Normally it would stop cold the instant you rewind back to the start of THIS room, because starting a new level clears the undo stack. allow_undo_level up in the Prelude skips that clearing, so a long enough undo chain here keeps going and walks you back through the previous room's final steps too.

section Status

#########
#P..k..d#
#########
MESSAGE [T4]: touching the Beacon wrote text to the status line via the "status" command - notice the game never paused for it the way a "message" command would have. Compare that to every popup back in the vanilla and PS+ files, all of which stopped play until you dismissed them.

section GrabBag

MESSAGE [T5] grab bag, part 1: gosub and log are rule-flow-control commands - gosub jumps into another rule group and can return, log just prints to the console - both about controlling RULES execution, not about messaging or level flow, so they only get a mention here. afx commands extend the sound-effect system past vanilla's fixed sfx0-sfx10 slots.

MESSAGE [T5] grab bag, part 2: mouse_clicks and auto_level_titles are new Prelude flags (mouse-driven input; auto-generated level names in menus). keyhint_color, title_color, and author_color add a few more cosmetic Prelude colors on top of vanilla's background_color/text_color.

MESSAGE [T5] grab bag, part 3: export_options trims title/footer/padding out of an exported standalone game.

MESSAGE [T5] grab bag, part 4: and everything from the PS+ file - level_select, section, goto, runtime_metadata_twiddling with noundo/norestart set/wipe/default, the in-rule undo/nosave/quit commands, message_text_align and its neighbors - still works completely unchanged here too.

MESSAGE That's the whole set across all three files - vanilla, PS+, and Next.
